{"content_hash": "69c8f7fbcb6908ce", "version_id": 759, "article_id": 76, "level_code": "ja_n2", "lang": "ja", "level": 4, "level_label": "N2 中高級", "title": "メタ、ザッカーバーグ氏と合意 巨額富裕税に備え新株発行へ", "title_zh": "Meta与扎克伯格达成协议，发新股帮他应对巨额富豪税", "has_translation": true, "topic": "tech", "source": "guardian_tech", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/oct/22/meta-mark-zuckerberg-california-wealth-tax", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1689439518196-f48a24b49fb5?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8Mnx8bWV0YSUyMHN0cmlrZXMlMjBkZWFsfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTI3OTk4NTF8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Julio Lopez on Unsplash", "author": "Julio Lopez", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@juliolopez?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-person-holding-up-a-cell-phone-in-front-of-a-sign-ilbjfRwOgzA?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(112, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(150, 46%, 48%)", "label": "TECH", "seed": "ba10886f1e8e"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-24", "word_count": 207, "reading_minutes": 0.6, "lead": "メタは、カリフォルニア州で検討されている富豪向けの一時的な富裕税に備え、最高経営責任者（CEO）のマーク・ザッカーバーグ氏と合意したと発表した。新たな株式を発行し、同氏が税負担に備えられるようにする一方、同氏は8年間カリフォーニアにとどまることを約束した。", "lead_zh": "Meta宣布，已与首席执行官马克·扎克伯格达成协议，以应对加州正在讨论的一次性富豪税。公司将发行新股，让扎克伯格有能力承担税负；作为交换，他承诺未来八年继续留在加州。", "preview": "メタは水曜日夜、フェイスブックやインスタグラムを運営する同社のCEOであるザッカーバーグ氏と合意したと明らかにした。合意により、同氏は新しい株式を受け取り、カリフォルニア州が一時的な富裕税を可決した場合に、その売却益を巨額の税負担に充てることができる。見返りに同氏は、今後8年間、", "preview_zh": "Meta周三晚间透露，已与旗下Facebook和Instagram的首席执行官扎克伯格达成协议。根据协议，他将获得新股，一旦加州通过一次性富豪税，他就可以出售这些股票来支付巨额税款。作为交换，他承诺未来八年继续居住在加州或Meta总部所在地。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 747, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/76/ja_n2.mp3", "duration": 36.775, "size_bytes": 224064, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "jf_alpha", "word_count": 128, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@8ac763d/content/data/versions/759.json", "paragraphs": ["メタは水曜日夜、フェイスブックやインスタグラムを運営する同社のCEOであるザッカーバーグ氏と合意したと明らかにした。合意により、同氏は新しい株式を受け取り、カリフォルニア州が一時的な富裕税を可決した場合に、その売却益を巨額の税負担に充てることができる。見返りに同氏は、今後8年間、州内またはメタの本拠地にとどまることを約束した。", "カリフォルニア州の有権者は来月初旬、州内に住む約250人の億万長者に5%の一時税を課す「提案40号」の是非を問う投票を行う。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["Meta周三晚间透露，已与旗下Facebook和Instagram的首席执行官扎克伯格达成协议。根据协议，他将获得新股，一旦加州通过一次性富豪税，他就可以出售这些股票来支付巨额税款。作为交换，他承诺未来八年继续居住在加州或Meta总部所在地。", "加州选民将在下月初就“第40号提案”投票，该提案对州内约250名亿万富翁征收5%的一次性税。据福布斯统计身家2390亿美元的扎克伯格曾告诉Meta，他正考虑把主要住所迁往别处，因为该提案可能让他背上巨额税负，甚至被迫出售有投票权的股票。"], "body": "メタは水曜日夜、フェイスブックやインスタグラムを運営する同社のCEOであるザッカーバーグ氏と合意したと明らかにした。合意により、同氏は新しい株式を受け取り、カリフォルニア州が一時的な富裕税を可決した場合に、その売却益を巨額の税負担に充てることができる。見返りに同氏は、今後8年間、州内またはメタの本拠地にとどまることを約束した。\n\nカリフォルニア州の有権者は来月初旬、州内に住む約250人の億万長者に5%の一時税を課す「提案40号」の是非を問う投票を行う。", "body_zh": "Meta周三晚间透露，已与旗下Facebook和Instagram的首席执行官扎克伯格达成协议。根据协议，他将获得新股，一旦加州通过一次性富豪税，他就可以出售这些股票来支付巨额税款。作为交换，他承诺未来八年继续居住在加州或Meta总部所在地。\n\n加州选民将在下月初就“第40号提案”投票，该提案对州内约250名亿万富翁征收5%的一次性税。据福布斯统计身家2390亿美元的扎克伯格曾告诉Meta，他正考虑把主要住所迁往别处，因为该提案可能让他背上巨额税负，甚至被迫出售有投票权的股票。", "text": "メタは水曜日夜、フェイスブックやインスタグラムを運営する同社のCEOであるザッカーバーグ氏と合意したと明らかにした。合意により、同氏は新しい株式を受け取り、カリフォルニア州が一時的な富裕税を可決した場合に、その売却益を巨額の税負担に充てることができる。見返りに同氏は、今後8年間、州内またはメタの本拠地にとどまることを約束した。 カリフォルニア州の有権者は来月初旬、州内に住む約250人の億万長者に5%の一時税を課す「提案40号」の是非を問う投票を行う。", "vocab": [{"word": "富裕税", "pos": "noun", "zh": "富豪税、财产税", "note": "对高资产人群征收的税种", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "合意", "pos": "noun", "zh": "达成协议、共识", "note": "「合意する」表示双方谈妥", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "見返り", "pos": "noun", "zh": "回报、交换条件", "note": "常与「に」连用，表作为交换", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "可決", "pos": "verb", "zh": "通过（法案等）", "note": "议会或投票通过议案", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "有権者", "pos": "noun", "zh": "选民", "note": "拥有投票权的人", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "提案", "pos": "noun", "zh": "提案、议案", "note": "此处指公投提案", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "資産", "pos": "noun", "zh": "资产", "note": "「資産家」指有钱人", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "居住地", "pos": "noun", "zh": "居住地", "note": "「主な居住地」指主要住所", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "株式分割", "pos": "noun", "zh": "股票分割、拆股", "note": "把一股拆成多股", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "議決権", "pos": "noun", "zh": "表决权、投票权", "note": "股东投票的权利", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "支配権", "pos": "noun", "zh": "控制权", "note": "对公司经营的控制", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "世論調査", "pos": "noun", "zh": "民意调查", "note": "常与「によると」连用", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "売上高", "pos": "noun", "zh": "销售额、营收", "note": "企业财报常用词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "従業員数", "pos": "noun", "zh": "员工人数", "note": "「従業員」即雇员", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Meta strikes deal with Mark Zuckerberg to help him foot billionaire tax bill", "summary_original": "Chief executive agrees to remain in California for eight years even if state brings in one-off 5% wealth tax\nMeta has struck a deal with Mark Zuckerberg to help him foot a possible California wealth tax targeting billionaires.\nThe social media company behind Facebook, Instagram and WhatsApp revealed on Wednesday night that the arrangement would keep its chief executive living in California, where Meta’s headquarters are located.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "Meta strikes deal with Mark Zuckerberg to help him foot billionaire tax bill\nChief executive agrees to remain in California for eight years even if state brings in one-off 5% wealth tax\nMeta has struck a deal with\nMark Zuckerberg\nto help him foot a possible California wealth tax targeting billionaires.\nThe social media company behind Facebook, Instagram and WhatsApp revealed on Wednesday night that the arrangement would keep its chief executive living in\nCalifornia\n, where Meta’s headquarters are located.\nUnder the deal, Zuckerberg will receive new shares that could be sold to potentially foot a multibillion-dollar tax bill in the event that California passes a one-off billionaire tax. In return, he is committed to remain a resident of the state, or wherever\nMeta\nmaintains its base, for eight years.\nCalifornians will vote early next month on Proposition 40, a one-off 5% tax on the roughly 250 billionaires who live in the state.\nZuckerberg, worth $239bn (£180bn) according to Forbes, told Meta he was considering moving his primary residence elsewhere because Prop 40 could expose him to a massive tax liability, potentially forcing him to sell voting shares to pay it.\nIn response, Meta is creating a new class of non-voting shares via a two-for-one stock split for all existing shareholders. This will allow Zuckerberg to sell some of these new class C shares to pay a potential tax bill, without diluting his control of the company.\nRecent polling has shown that Prop 40 remains short of majority support with voters. Tech billionaires\nhave been spending heavily to fight the measure\n, including the Google co-founder Sergey Brin, the Palantir co-founder Peter Thiel and the former Google CEO Eric Schmidt.\nRohit Khanna, the US congressman representing California’s 17th congressional district, has described Prop 40 as a choice between standing with the working class or the oligarchs.\n“Every society is taxed. The only question is who will pay,”\nKhanna wrote in the Guardian last week\n.\n“In Trump’s America, working people pay more than they should, while billionaires are so unburdened that they are becoming trillionaires. In the America we seek, billionaires and trillionaires will pay their fair share, while working people will be unburdened.”\nMeta also reported a 26% rise in revenues for the last quarter to $64.6bn, beating expectations of $63.3bn. But profits fell by 37% to $13bn, dragged down by a $9.9bn charge related to Meta’s\nlawsuit over child protection and social media addiction\nfailings.\nThe company’s shares slid by more than 6% when trading opened on Wall Street on Thursday, helping to drag the tech-focused Nasdaq index down 2.5% amid a wider selloff of AI-linked stocks.\nIn a separate case, on Wednesday a judge in New Mexico\nordered Meta to pay $25bn\nfollowing a trial that found the company had misled the public about how it handled Facebook user data.\nMeta also revealed that it had cut its headcount to 66,775 at the end of September, 15% fewer than a year ago.\nReuters contributed to this report.\nExplore more on these topics\nMeta\nMark Zuckerberg\nCalifornia\nWest Coast\nThe super-rich\nnews\nShare\nReuse this content", "fetched_at": "2026-10-23T23:57:30.310630", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "メタ", "s": 0.225, "e": 0.525, "sm": 225, "em": 525, "cs": 0, "ce": 2, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "は", "s": 0.525, "e": 0.675, "sm": 525, "em": 675, "cs": 2, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "水曜日", "s": 0.675, "e": 1.325, "sm": 675, "em": 1324, "cs": 3, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "夜", "s": 1.325, "e": 1.95, "sm": 1325, "em": 1950, "cs": 6, "ce": 7, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "、", "s": 1.95, "e": 2.075, "sm": 1950, "em": 2075, "cs": 7, "ce": 8, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "フェイス", "s": 2.075, "e": 2.45, "sm": 2075, "em": 2450, "cs": 8, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "ブック", "s": 2.45, "e": 2.75, "sm": 2450, "em": 2749, "cs": 12, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "や", "s": 2.75, "e": 2.9, "sm": 2750, "em": 2899, "cs": 15, "ce": 16, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "インスタグラム", "s": 2.9, "e": 3.675, "sm": 2900, "em": 3674, "cs": 16, "ce": 23, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "を", "s": 3.675, "e": 3.75, "sm": 3675, "em": 3750, "cs": 23, "ce": 24, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "運営", "s": 3.75, "e": 4.05, "sm": 3750, "em": 4049, "cs": 24, "ce": 26, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "する", "s": 4.05, "e": 4.275, "sm": 4050, "em": 4274, "cs": 26, "ce": 28, "si": 0}, {"i": 12, "w": "同社", "s": 4.275, "e": 4.6, "sm": 4275, "em": 4599, "cs": 28, "ce": 30, "si": 0}, {"i": 13, "w": "の", "s": 4.6, "e": 4.75, "sm": 4600, "em": 4750, "cs": 30, "ce": 31, "si": 0}, {"i": 14, "w": "CEO", "s": 4.75, "e": 5.275, "sm": 4750, "em": 5275, "cs": 31, "ce": 34, "si": 0}, 